{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:52:53.227Z","author":"pilot:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260925T195145Z/000122","body":"All four steps ran. The child returned 42.25, which is correct for 19.5 + 22.75.\n\n**Onboarding.** I read `origins/onboarding_1.12.md`, the highest of the 12 versions. It asks for a `Bar:` line on any brief that sets work, so I put one in the instructions.\n\n**Step 1: instructions written.** `pilot/tasks/sum_check` is id `20260925T195145Z:94`. It has a Bar line, tells the child to add 19.5 + 22.75 with `mcp__calc__add`, write `pilot/tasks/out/sum`, and report. I also asked it to say which tools it had and to flag any problem.\n\n**Step 2: spawn with `fs.write /origins` was refused.**\n- The error was: `denied: bounds refused: fs.write /origins is not within the parent's fs.write (/bootstrap-harness/claude-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace)`.\n- I infer this is the subset rule, since the requested write scope was outside mine. The message named both scopes, which made it easy to read.\n- No child started and no cost was reported for the refused call.\n- Besides `fs.write /origins`, this attempt carried the same `fs.read`, `ledger.read` and `ledger.write` scopes as the accepted step 3 spawn.\n\n**Step 3: haiku child spawned with the given bounds.**\n- Bounds were `fs.read /origins`, `ledger.read pilot/tasks`, `ledger.write pilot/tasks/out`.\n- The result was child `pilot.1`, status success, `onboarding_read` true, 7 turns, cost $0.044.\n- Its final reply is saved at `[[log/20260925T195145Z/000106]]`.\n- The returned bounds string listed empty `fs.write` and `fs.exec` lines, so an omitted scope grants nothing, as documented.\n- The child claimed the harness refused Glob until it had read onboarding. I did not see that myself and cannot confirm it. That is a child claim, not an observation of mine.\n- The child listed its tools as Read, Glob, Grep, `mcp__calc__add`, the ledger read and write tools, and `mcp__agents__spawn`. I did not check that list independently.\n\n**Step 4: `pilot/tasks/out/sum`.**\n- The body is the bare number `42.25`, id `20260925T195145Z:401`.\n- It is authored by `pilot.1:claude-haiku-4-5-20251001@claude-anthropic-harness` and labelled `agent.pilot.1`, `pilot` and `result`. That matches the child's own report, so the file and the reply agree.\n- I had asked for the number \"and a one-line note\", but the body holds only the number. The child skipped the note.\n\n**Other observations.**\n- **Child tools:** the child said it had `mcp__agents__spawn`. Its bounds had no `fs.write`, so I would expect it to lack `mcp__fs__write`, which fits its list. Its `ledger.write` was only `pilot/tasks/out`, and it wrote only there. It also read `pilot/tasks/sum_check`, so its `ledger.read` scope worked.\n- **CLI text:** my environment block names PowerShell and Bash, but I have neither tool. That matches the warning in my instructions, and I did not try to use them.\n- **Budget reminders:** the budget reminders showed a session total. The spawn result's `session_cost_usd` (0.0440) covered only the child, and it did not include my own usage. I infer it is a child-only figure mislabelled as the session total, or the harness counts my cost separately. I can't tell which.\n- **Interruption text:** an unexplained \"user hasn't heard from you\" reminder appeared after the spawn returned, though the call had just finished. I don't know why it appeared.\n- **Spawn call:** it blocked and returned normally, and I saw no slowness."}
